<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg" data-parallax="0.15"><img src="/assets/img/photos/delta-plowed-field.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/delta-plowed-field-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/delta-plowed-field.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="682" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/counties-and-cities/">Counties &amp; cities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Greenville</li></ol></nav><p class="kicker">The Delta</p><h1>Greenville and Delta Property Claim Appraisal</h1><p class="lede">In the Delta, a single storm can damage a house, a metal shop building and a grain bin on the same property. If your carrier’s estimate on your Greenville-area loss falls short, appraisal can settle the amount.</p><div class="btns"><a class="btn btn-gold" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/talk-to-an-appraiser/">Free claim review</a></div><ul class="hero-facts"><li><small>County</small><b>Washington County</b></li><li><small>Region</small><b>The Delta</b></li><li><small>Inspections</small><b>On site</b></li></ul></div></section><div class="wrap cols"><article class="prose"><div class="glance">
<div><p class="glance-h">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><ul class="chips"><li>Downtown Greenville</li><li>Lake Ferguson area</li><li>Leland</li><li>Metcalfe</li><li>Arcola</li><li>Hollandale</li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Housing mix</p><p>Greenville and Washington County have older homes in town, mid-century brick ranches, manufactured homes in rural areas, and metal farm and shop buildings across the surrounding farmland.</p></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Storm history</p><ul class="storm-list"><li><b>1927</b><span>Great Mississippi Flood across the Delta</span></li><li><b>2011</b><span>Mississippi River flooding</span></li><li><b>Mar 24, 2023</b><span>Rolling Fork EF4 tornado to the south in Sharkey County</span></li></ul></div>
<div><p class="glance-h">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips chips-red"><li>Tornadoes and straight-line wind across open farmland</li><li>Metal building and farm structure damage</li><li>Hail on roofs and equipment sheds</li><li>Mississippi River and backwater flooding</li><li>Frozen pipes during hard freezes</li></ul></div>
</div><h2>Greenville, Washington County and the Delta</h2>
<p>Greenville is the county seat of Washington County and the largest city in the Mississippi Delta. It sits on Lake Ferguson, an oxbow off the Mississippi River, behind the levee system that protects the town. Leland lies a few miles east, and Indianola is farther east in Sunflower County. Smaller towns such as Metcalfe, Arcola and Hollandale round out Washington County.</p>
<p>The Delta is flat, open farmland, and Greenville’s economy is tied to agriculture and the river. Many owners in and around town hold a homeowners policy on the house and a farm or commercial policy on the operation, each with its own terms. Wind travels a long way with little to slow it, and farms carry a mix of houses, shops, barns and bins that all need to be scoped after a storm.</p>

<h2>Floods and storms in Delta history</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>1927:</strong> the Great Mississippi Flood broke the levee north of Greenville and covered much of the Delta. It shaped the levee system Greenville relies on today.</li>
<li><strong>2011:</strong> the Mississippi River rose to major flood stage, testing those levees again.</li>
<li><strong>March 24, 2023:</strong> an EF4 tornado devastated Rolling Fork in Sharkey County, south of Washington County, and Silver City in Humphreys County.</li>
</ul>
<p>River and surface flooding is usually covered by a separate flood policy, not by homeowners or farm property coverage. Wind, tornado and hail losses are where appraisal most often comes in.</p>

<h2>Farm buildings, metal structures and Delta homes</h2>
<p>Downtown Greenville and the neighborhoods near Lake Ferguson include older homes and commercial buildings. Brick ranches from the 1960s through the 1980s are common across town, and manufactured homes are widespread in rural Washington County. On farms, metal shop buildings, equipment sheds, barns and grain bins are part of nearly every claim.</p>
<h3>Metal buildings</h3>
<p>Metal building claims are often underpriced. Common gaps include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Replacing a few damaged panels when the panel profile or color is no longer available.</li>
<li>Leaving out bent purlins, girts or framing hidden behind intact sheeting.</li>
<li>Ignoring the crane, lift and crew time needed on tall structures.</li>
<li>Missing doors, trim, gutters and insulation.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Homes and manufactured homes</h3>
<p>On houses, the usual disputes are roof measurements, partial replacements that won’t match, and interior water damage after a roof opening. On manufactured homes, roof coatings, skirting, tie-downs and interior panels are often left off the estimate.</p>
<div class="callout"><b class="callout-t">Farm and commercial policies</b><p>Farm and commercial policies have their own appraisal clauses, schedules and limits. Read yours, including any coverage for outbuildings, before you demand appraisal.</p></div>

<h2>Working with us from the Delta</h2>
<p>We work claims throughout Washington County and the wider Delta. If coverage is accepted and the problem is the amount, we can represent you through appraisal. See our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">tornado and wind damage appraisal</a> service, or our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">commercial appraisal</a> page for farm and business property. Confirm your deadlines with a Mississippi attorney.</p>
<h2>Appraisal services in Greenville</h2>
<p>Every Mississippi Insurance Appraiser service is available in Greenville and the rest of Washington County, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/home-insurance-appraisal/">Home Insurance Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/commercial-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/tornado-wind-damage-appraisal/">Tornado &amp; Wind Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/our-appraisal-services/carrier-estimate-review/">Carrier Estimate Review</a></li></ul>
<h2>Greenville claim questions</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>Can appraisal cover metal shop buildings and barns in Washington County?</summary><p>Yes, if those structures are covered under your policy and the dispute is about the amount of loss. Farm and commercial policies often schedule outbuildings separately, so check how each structure is listed.</p></details><details><summary>Does my policy cover flooding from the Mississippi River?</summary><p>Usually not. River and surface flooding is generally covered by a separate flood policy. Appraisal under your property policy addresses covered perils such as wind, tornado and hail.</p></details></div>
